# `takes(.., () => f(1), pick(i))`: Link lets `f` count as only called: the arrow goes to a function in sight, in its own block of the body. The walk copies
# pick() in line between the making and the call, which parts them into two blocks of the Code, so the sweep lends nothing: the arrow is made in the heap, in
# every turn, and brings `f`, which may lie in a caller's frame, to the heap first. What it brings remembers its copy, so the chain behind it is copied once.
# -- source: closure-parted-from-its-call-by-a-copy-in-line-brings-its-capture-to-the-heap.ts
